00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:44.400
 but opposing network designed for peacetime operations.

00:35:44.400 --> 00:35:45.200
 Yes, it does.

00:35:45.200 --> 00:35:48.240
 And this brings us to the third phase of our physiological hack.

00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:51.840
 The parasympathetic nervous system or the PSNS.

00:35:52.560 --> 00:35:55.680
 This is the yin to the sympathetic nervous system's yang.

00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:58.880
 If the SNS is about immediate explosive survival,

00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:03.200
 the parasympathetic system is entirely focused on conservation,

00:36:03.200 --> 00:36:05.920
 recovery, digestion, and baseline maintenance.

00:36:06.480 --> 00:36:09.200
 It's the janitorial staff in the maintenance crew of the body.

00:36:09.200 --> 00:36:09.760
 Exactly.

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:14.640
 The source material introduces a class of drugs designed to hack this system

00:36:14.640 --> 00:36:16.720
 called colonergic drugs,

00:36:16.720 --> 00:36:21.040
 also known as colonergic agonists or parasympathymometics.

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:24.880
 And just as the adrenergic drugs mimicked catacolamines,

00:36:24.880 --> 00:36:28.320
 these drugs mimic the effects of the PSNS neurotransmitter,

00:36:28.320 --> 00:36:30.640
 which is called acetylcholine or ACH.

00:36:31.200 --> 00:36:35.360
 Acetylcholine is the master chemical of the rest and digest state,

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:37.920
 where adrenaline screams acetylcholine whispers.

00:36:38.640 --> 00:36:41.520
 The notes outline two completely different mechanisms of action

00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:44.240
 for how these drugs increase the parasympathetic signal.

00:36:44.960 --> 00:36:47.680
 First, there are direct-acting colonergic agonists.

00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:49.680
 These are pretty straightforward.

00:36:49.680 --> 00:36:52.960
 They just bind directly to the colonergic receptors on the cells

00:36:52.960 --> 00:36:56.080
 and activate them, just like a synthetic key in the lock.

00:36:56.080 --> 00:36:58.560
 And just like the agogenics we talked about earlier.

00:36:58.560 --> 00:36:58.880
 Right.

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:02.720
 But then there are indirect-acting colonergic agonists,

00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:06.240
 which are also known as colonesterase inhibitors.

00:37:06.240 --> 00:37:10.800
 And the mechanism for the indirect actors is one of the coolest biochemical hacks we have.

00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:12.400
 Right, because looking at the word,

00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:15.840
 esterase usually means an enzyme that breaks something apart, right?

00:37:16.480 --> 00:37:21.200
 So acetylcholine esterase is the natural enzyme that acts as the cleanup crew,

00:37:21.200 --> 00:37:23.680
 sweeping up all the acetylcholine in the synapses.

00:37:23.680 --> 00:37:26.080
 So the signal doesn't just last forever.

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:27.280
 Precisely.

00:37:27.280 --> 00:37:30.960
 If direct-acting drugs are like hiring 100 extra workers to do a job,

00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:34.240
 indirect-acting drugs take a totally different approach.

00:37:34.240 --> 00:37:37.760
 They just fire the managers who usually send the normal workers home.

00:37:37.760 --> 00:37:40.720
 By inhibiting the enzyme that destroys acetylcholine,

00:37:40.720 --> 00:37:44.240
 you don't actually add any synthetic drug to the receptor.

00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:47.360
 You just let the body's own natural supply of acetylcholine build up.

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:50.400
 Pool in the synapses and continuously fire,

00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:53.360
 which massively amplifies the parasympathetic signal.

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:56.240
 So what does that amplified signal actually force the body to do?

00:37:57.520 --> 00:38:01.840
 The rest and digest effects detailed in our notes are extensive.

00:38:02.640 --> 00:38:06.080
 And they are the exact mirror opposite of the adrenaline rush.

00:38:06.080 --> 00:38:07.280
 Completely opposite, yeah.

00:38:08.080 --> 00:38:12.720
 It stimulates the intestine and bladder, causing increased gastric secretions,

00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:17.360
 massive increases in gastrointestinal motility, and increased urinary frequency.

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:22.320
 It stimulates the pupils, causing intense constriction or meiosis,

00:38:22.320 --> 00:38:26.000
 which the notes point out actually reduces intraocular pressure in the eye.

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:28.080
 Which is why they're used for glaucoma sometimes.

00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:28.320
 Right.

00:38:29.200 --> 00:38:31.360
 It causes increased salivation and sweating.

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:36.720
 On the cardiovascular side, it forces a decreased heart rate and vasodilation.

00:38:37.360 --> 00:38:41.920
 And for respiratory, it causes bronchial constriction and narrowed airways.

00:38:41.920 --> 00:38:44.160
 It is a total systemic stand-down.

00:38:44.720 --> 00:38:47.600
 The heart rate plummets, the blood pressure softens,

00:38:48.400 --> 00:38:51.760
 the digestive tract, which was totally frozen during the bear attack,

00:38:51.760 --> 00:38:56.080
 suddenly surges to life, churning and secreting acids to process food.

00:38:56.080 --> 00:38:57.440
 The maintenance crew is working.

00:38:57.440 --> 00:39:00.960
 Yeah, the bladder aggressively signals that it's time to empty.

00:39:00.960 --> 00:39:04.480
 And the pupils shrink down to tiny pinpricks because you are safe.

00:39:04.480 --> 00:39:09.440
 You don't need to scan the horizon for predators while you're just eating a meal or taking a nap.

00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:14.160
 The material makes a very important distinction regarding the receptors these drugs target though.

00:39:14.160 --> 00:39:17.360
 It states that at recommended therapeutic doses,

00:39:17.360 --> 00:39:20.720
 colonergic drugs primarily affect muscarinic receptors,

00:39:20.720 --> 00:39:23.920
 which provides all those desired clinical effects we just listed.

00:39:23.920 --> 00:39:24.400
 Right.

00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:29.520
 But if the dose gets too high, they start spilling over and stimulating nicotinic receptors,

00:39:29.520 --> 00:39:32.560
 which causes a cascade of highly undesirable side effects.

00:39:32.560 --> 00:39:33.280
 Right.

00:39:33.280 --> 00:39:37.920
 Muscarinic receptors are your main target for smooth, therapeutic, rest and digest functions.

00:39:38.480 --> 00:39:41.440
 Nicotinic receptors are a different beast entirely.

